{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PTWN7LgGv6bcpMxG9LsGmB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, the PRUNE_SHMEM_KERNELS flag is set in build.rs and applies globally to ALL CUDA files. This means even the non-batched per-AIR kernels only have NEEDS_SHMEM=false variants.\n\nFor the benchmark with l_skip=4 (skip_domain=16), this is safe because 16 <= WARP_SIZE=32. But could there be some kernel that needs NEEDS_SHMEM=true for a reason other than skip_domain?\n\nLet me check: the NEEDS_SHMEM flag is used in the `ntt_eval_dag_entry` template function. \n\nWith skip_domain=16, all coset values fit within a single warp, so shared memory isn't required for inter-warp communication. But I should verify whether the GKR input evaluation kernels also depend on this flag.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":163287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":884},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"694fb196-69bb-4e1f-a777-5a160503c446","uuid":"73987c1b-3db1-4631-bd83-d221f29ea728"}
