{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0159LkragyWQi48Nqe5rZVnR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-1600-fix-batch-round0-revert-and-reapply\n2\t\n3\tRevert the broken batch-round0-descriptors commit (0d1bb2f9) which causes APC 300 STARK proving to hang for 12+ minutes, then re-apply the batch Round 0 path with the CPU bottleneck fixed. The existing batch code redundantly reconstructs logup interaction DAGs and rules per batchable AIR via `build_logup_rules_for_air()` (involving `SymbolicDagBuilder`, `SymbolicRulesGpu::new`, and per-AIR device uploads), which takes prohibitively long for the ~300 small AIRs at APC 300. The fix reuses the precomputed `logup_round0_buffer_size` from `AirDataGpu` and the existing per-AIR logup rule data (DAG, rules, weights) that the non-batched path already constructs during Phase 1 work-item preparation, avoiding all redundant CPU-side symbolic computation.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JPA4RSMeQ3tv79eo7vUE4f","session_id":"694fb196-69bb-4e1f-a777-5a160503c446","uuid":"0a6a8419-b945-4793-90c6-ad0ec9ee8ec5","timestamp":"2026-04-15T14:19:50.343Z"}
